Avoid NULL bytes tricks:
========================
1)
mov ecx, 2

is 5 bytes with NULLs: B9 02 00 00 00
we can change it to:

push 02
pop ecx

6A02 --> push 02
59   --> pop ecx

2) use negative value then negate it

example:

mov eax, 1C6h  --> B8 C6 01 00 00
instead you can negate 1C6h:
? 0x00 - 0x1C6 = fffffe3a

change code to:

mov eax, fffffe3a
neg eax

3) if we want to use 0 value:
mov dword ptr fs:[0], esp

to avoid zero number, we can xor itself some register and use the register value:

xor ebx, ebx 
mov dword ptr fs:[ebx], esp

4) add to 32 bit register constant number

mov eax, [esp+0c]

you can change to:

push 0x0c     
pop ecx     
mov eax, [esp+ecx]
